# Copy to .env.local for development. Never commit .env.local.

# --- Database (Phase 03) ---------------------------------------------------
# Postgres connection string. Everything degrades gracefully without it:
#   POST /api/leads answers 503 so the client falls back to composing an email
#   POST /api/quiz  answers { ok: true, stored: false } and the page carries on
# There is one connection string — Postgres is local to the VPS, so no
# pooled/unpooled split (§6.1).
DATABASE_URL=postgres://USER:PASSWORD@localhost:5432/rem_assist

# --- Lead notification (§9.3) ----------------------------------------------
# Webhook that receives a plain-text summary on every lead. A Slack incoming
# webhook works as-is. Unset = notifications are skipped silently.
# LEAD_WEBHOOK_URL=

# --- Site (§11) ------------------------------------------------------------
# Origin used for canonicals, OG urls and the sitemap. Defaults to
# https://remassistance.com — set this on staging so its pages do not declare
# production canonicals.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://staging.remassistance.com

# --- Analytics -------------------------------------------------------------
# There are two ways to measure this site and you want exactly one of them.
#
# 1. A Google Tag Manager container, e.g. GTM-XXXXXXX. Tags — including a GA4
#    configuration tag — are then added in the GTM UI, and this app only
#    pushes events into the container. Leave unset and no container loads at
#    all: components/analytics/GoogleTagManager.tsx renders null without it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID=
# 2. The GA4 measurement id on its own, e.g. G-XXXXXXXXXX — gtag.js loaded
#    directly by components/analytics/GoogleAnalytics.tsx, no container. The
#    property for remassistance.com is G-Q0FWM76FTF.
#
# SETTING BOTH DOES NOT LAYER THEM. A GA4 tag in the container plus this one
# on the page counts every page view and every conversion twice, which looks
# plausible in a report and is not. So GTM wins: whenever NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID
# is set, the direct tag renders null and this variable is ignored.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=
# The production gate. Events are only emitted — and, with option 2, the tag
# only loads at all — when this is exactly 'production' (see
# lib/analytics/events.ts). Set it in the *Production scope only* in the
# Vercel dashboard, and in shared/.env on the VPS. Leave it unset locally and
# in CI: the site works, the banner works, nothing is measured. To check a tag
# from a laptop, set it here together with the id above and accept in the
# banner — the hits land in the real property, so do it deliberately.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined at build time, not read at runtime. On the VPS that
# is fine only because deploy/remote-deploy.sh sources shared/.env before it
# runs `next build` — move the build anywhere else and this silently becomes
# undefined, with no error to tell you analytics has gone dark.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_ENV=production
# Consent gate. 'opt-in' (the default when unset) stores nothing — no
# attribution cookie, no tags — until the visitor accepts. Set to 'off' ONLY
# if this site does not serve EEA or UK visitors: it removes the banner and
# grants everything. That is a legal decision, not a performance one.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONSENT_MODE=opt-in

# --- Backend API -------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the NestJS backend (remassist-backend) listens. Used by server
# components and middleware directly, and by the /api/v1/* proxy in
# next.config.ts (rewrites are compiled at build time, so this must be set
# when `next build` runs). Admin sign-in, sessions and accounts live there.
API_URL=http://localhost:4000

# --- Uploads (Phase 04 team CMS) ---------------------------------------------
# Where team headshots are written on disk, relative to an absolute base. The
# public URL is /uploads/team/<uuid>.<ext> (served by a route handler), so on
# the VPS point this at a persistent directory — e.g. /var/rem-assist/uploads —
# that survives redeploys. Default (unset) is <project>/.uploads/team.
# UPLOAD_DIR=/var/rem-assist/uploads
